/* The sentence a person reads when the system asks for a permission. The system localises
   its own half — the title and the buttons — and shows THIS half exactly as written, so a
   phrase without a translation reaches every language unchanged. The source is English
   (Info.plist); this file is one language of it. */

"NSCameraUsageDescription" = "Montana 使用相机在聊天中拍摄照片和视频、录制视频消息、进行视频通话，以及扫描他人的二维码。";
"NSContactsUsageDescription" = "Montana 使用通讯录，以便你在聊天中分享联系人，并按 @名称将你在 Montana 中添加的人保存到通讯录。可在设置的隐私中关闭“同步联系人”。";
"NSFaceIDUsageDescription" = "Montana 使用面容 ID 显示你的 24 个恢复词。";
"NSLocationWhenInUseUsageDescription" = "Montana 使用你的位置，以便你在聊天中发送它。";
"NSMicrophoneUsageDescription" = "Montana 使用麦克风录制语音消息、视频和通话。";
"NSPhotoLibraryAddUsageDescription" = "Montana 将聊天中的照片保存到你的相册。";
"NSPhotoLibraryUsageDescription" = "Montana 显示你最近的照片和视频，以便快速发送。";

/* The name iCloud gives this app's storage (NSUbiquitousContainers in Info.plist). The iCloud
   daemon keeps that name per language and takes each language's name from THIS file only (read
   in its own code, 23.09): without this line the container carried a name in no language at all,
   while Apple's storage page called it "app", the tail of the container's identifier. The
   product's name is one word in every language. */
"NSUbiquitousContainerName" = "Montana";
